  "id": "rodalmighty",
  "neon": "#5cc7e8",
  "note": "ROD ALMIGHTY — the tackle shop on Meltwater Row, across the road from the bronze fisherman.\n\nThe tile's prose: rods standing in the window in a rank, tips up; a whiteboard by the door with the\nweek's water in a cramped hand (what's running, where, what they're taking); the sign ROD ALMIGHTY\nand under it, smaller, IF HE COULD DO IT SO CAN YOU.\n\nSo the shop window is a tall bay with close vertical glazing bars that read as the rods, the door\nbeside it under a short hood, the whiteboard on the pier between them, and the two-line sign on a fascia. The\nbuilding is painted timber boarding over a brick plinth, with a lit flat upstairs.",
